<title>USA: Brent crude inches up in light U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude inches up in light U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude oil inched up in light U.S. paper trading late on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>Four partial August cargoes changed hands a total of 300 times between $17.64 and $17.68 a barrel</p>
<p>August Brent on the IPE settled at $17.63 a barrel.</p>
<p>July/August Brent traded once at minus 19.5 cents, going out at minus 20/19 cents.</p>
<p>August/September was pegged at the same level.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
